From 36c70cd566860c44557adb146c730f4f53b9774e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vdn-h100 <none@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:31:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] vdn: render resolution as a config field

480P does not exist upstream: src/inference/render.py hardcodes
LATENT_H, LATENT_W = 48, 84 -- the 768x1344 production canvas -- as a module
constant, and both Ulysses and single-GPU entrypoints inherit it.

Everything downstream of that constant is already resolution-agnostic: the
window softmax bounds are per frame, the packed layout carries its own spatial
grid, and Ulysses shards by row with padding on the last rank. So this only
lifts the constant into render.height / render.width and threads the resulting
latent canvas through generate_latents, with latent_grid() rejecting anything
that is not a multiple of 32 (the 16x spatial VAE, then the transformer's 2x2
patch) rather than silently truncating a row of tokens.

Defaults are unchanged: render.height/width default to 768/1344 and
latent_hw=None keeps the released grid, so an existing config renders exactly
what it rendered before.

H3-Base is trained at 768p, so any other canvas is out of distribution -- it
renders, but there is no reference output to compare against.
